  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> is initially at rest at the origin. It is subjected to a force and starts moving along the x - axis. Its kinetic energy changes with time as <math><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where <math><mi>&#947;</mi></math> is a positive constant of appropriate dimensions. Which of the following statements is (are) true?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "The force applied on the particle is constant",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The speed of the particle is proportional to time",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The distance of the particle from the origin increases linearly with time",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Since force is constant, it is conservative.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given the change in kinetic energy<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>.</p><p>Kinetic energy is expressed as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br />Integrating the above relation,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mi>t</mi><mo>;</mo><mrow> <mi>&#965;</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow> </math> ... (i)<br /><math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math><br />Since <math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>m</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math></p>"
  }
